//! Recognizer: rules_dotnet (design 2.7). The NuGet packages of a
//! rules_dotnet build are the `nuget_repo(...)` entries of a file that
//! `paket2bazel` generates, one per Paket group: `paket.<group>.bzl`.
//! Nothing else is read by the build: not `packages.lock.json`, not
//! `nuget.config`, not `paket.lock` itself.
//!
//! A hub is found by the generated file's name, where the build loads it:
//!
//! - Bzlmod: `use_extension("//<pkg>:paket.<group>_extension.bzl", ...)`
//!   on a file of the main repository. That file is generated as well, and
//!   its one `load` names the data file.
//! - `WORKSPACE`: `load("//<pkg>:paket.<group>.bzl", "<group>")` and a
//!   call of the loaded function.
//!
//! The generator's output changed four times, and each change decides
//! something (read at the tags named, `tools/paket2bazel/Gen.fs` and
//! `dotnet/private/sdk/gen/NugetRepo.fs`):
//!
//! | Release | Files | First statement | Entries |
//! |---|---|---|---|
//! | 0.8 - 0.9 | one `paket.bzl` | `"Generated by paket2bazel"` | tuples |
//! | 0.10 - 0.12 | one `paket.bzl` for every group | the same | dicts |
//! | 0.13 - 0.14 | a data file and an extension file per group | the same, in both | dicts |
//! | 0.15 - 0.22.2 | the same pair | `"GENERATED"`, `"Generated"` | dicts with `"name"` first |
//!
//! The fourth change is in the extension file: from 0.19.0 it returns
//! `extension_metadata(reproducible = True)`, so Bazel keeps no entry for
//! it in `MODULE.bazel.lock`. Before that it does, and an edit of the data
//! file stales the entry's `bzlTransitiveDigest` (probe U3: an `error`-mode
//! build then fails with `... or one of its transitive .bzl files has
//! changed`). Which of the two a workspace has is read off the committed
//! files, the lock first and the literal in the extension file second:
//! the rules_dotnet version says what the generator *would* write, and the
//! committed pair may be older than the ruleset.
//!
//! Only a per-group file of dict lines is a shape a lane edits. The single
//! `paket.bzl` and the tuple format are recognized so that they are
//! refused by name, and anything this reader does not know is
//! [`PaketData::Unknown`]. The file is the generator's, not the user's: a
//! later `paket2bazel` run writes it again from `paket.lock` and the NuGet
//! cache and drops a pin without a word (probe U3), so the spans kept
//! here are for an edit a lane must also be able to find undone.
//!
//! Under `WORKSPACE` the archive of a package is one repository for every
//! group, `nuget.<id>.v<version>`, declared through `maybe`: the first
//! group that lists the package decides its bytes (read at v0.14.0 and
//! v0.22.2 `dotnet/private/rules/nuget/nuget_repo.bzl`). The hubs are
//! therefore listed in the order of their calls, with the groups of other
//! repositories that are called before them.
//!
//! A generated extension of another module is that module's hub, and its
//! files are not in this tree. The ruleset with no group of the root that
//! was read is a `RulesetSignal`: Bazel may build NuGet packages from a
//! file this reader did not find. Liveness and the ruleset version are
//! `govern`'s to decide; every hub leaves with the version unknown.

